# Context

## Background
The T066 handoff in to-do.json named three blockers found during the
2026-09-14 evaluation. A three-agent comprehension workflow on
2026-09-15 confirmed each with file:line evidence before this fix.

## Why This Way
- The configure point is the CLI dispatcher, not each handler: one
  site covers replay, probe, trace import, eval, evaluate, report,
  and study init, and commands with their own table (run, serve,
  doctor) reconfigure afterwards. Last writer wins; one process
  resolves one table, so no cross-contamination is observable today.
- The exposure got a real GatewayState rather than a private promise
  chain: serializeState is the sanctioned ordering mechanism, the
  state ledger only records stage/commit/rollback of operation keys
  (no hidden backend behavior), and the stateful mock work (T069)
  builds on exactly this.
- @oal/report gained a dependency on @oal/config for
  schemaWorkerSettingsOf; the mapping stays in config so core keeps
  no dependency on the table type.

## Gotchas
- configureSchemaWorker mutates one process-global singleton. If a
  future feature runs concurrent exposures with DIFFERENT tables in
  one process, the last configure wins and settings bleed across
  exposures; per-call settings would be needed then.
- grade() in doctor.ts is a nested function so the finally that
  closes the worker still returns the graded check.
